TSK-101 **Review of the diff summary & commit message**

**Commit purpose**  
The change addresses **TSK‑101**: “API: duplicate booking 500 → clean 409”. The goal is to replace an internal‑server‑error response (HTTP 500) with a proper client‑error response (HTTP 409 Conflict) when a duplicate booking is attempted.

**Key modifications**

| File | Change summary |
|------|----------------|
| `.agent-loop/backlog-inbox.md`, `.agent-loop/loop-stdout.log`, `.agent-loop/loop.log`, `.agent-loop/run-TSK-101.log` | Logging/artifact files – no impact on compiled code. |
| `apps/api/Sources/App/Controllers/BookingController.swift` | Small edit (‑8 lines, +8 lines) to catch the new `BookingError.duplicate` case and return `409`. |
| `apps/api/Sources/App/Errors/BookingError.swift` | **+18 lines** – introduces a new `enum BookingError: Error` case `duplicate` (and possibly other cases). |
| `apps/api/Sources/App/Extensions/ErrorHandlerExtensions.swift` | **+11 lines** – adds mapping from `BookingError.duplicate` to `HTTPResponseStatus.conflict` (409). |
| `apps/api/Tests/App/Tests/BookingControllerTests.swift` | **+37 lines** – new unit test verifying that a duplicate booking request yields a 409 response. |
| `apps/api/Tests/AppTests/BookingErrorTests.swift` | **+19 lines** – tests for the new `BookingError` mapping. |
